{
  "sample": "internet-python-flask-realworld",
  "$comment": "Hand-labeled from the pinned sample source (scripts/samples.json), not from Concentrate output. gothinkster/flask-realworld-example-app. Routes: every `@blueprint.route(path, methods=(..))` of the three views modules (articles, user, profile), one label per method with the path as written (the paths are absolute: the blueprints have no url_prefix and `register_blueprints` in conduit/app.py registers them without one) and the line of the decorator. Flask's `<converter:name>` syntax is kept as written. Data access (Phase 32): every `Model.query\u2026`, `self.query\u2026`, `Model(...)` / typed `.save()` / `.delete()` of the CRUD mixin in a function of conduit/, one label per (function, model, operation). The mixin's own `save` / `delete` / `get_by_id` act on whichever model has the mixin and are not labelled. A `.save()` on a value the code reaches through a relationship (`current_user.profile.save()`, `article.comments\u2026first().delete()`) is labelled although its model is not named. Env: the two `os.environ.get` reads of conduit/settings.py (`request.headers.environ[...]` in conduit/user/views.py is a WSGI dict, not the process environment). Calls (Phase 33): every call site of conduit/ whose callee name is a function, method or class written in the repository, listed with Python's own ast module and decided by reading the code, not from the tool's output; nested functions (execute_tool in conduit/commands.py) count as written in the repository. A call of a class runs its __init__ (the class itself when it has none: the marshmallow schemas); db.Model.__init__ and Exception.__init__ run library code (target null). .save / .update / .delete on a model run CRUDMixin in conduit/extensions.py, the model_class passed to SQLAlchemy(model_class=CRUDMixin), and so do the calls through current_user.profile; User.get_by_id runs SurrogatePK.get_by_id. error.to_json in the errorhandler is registered for InvalidUsage at runtime and is marked dynamic. Library calls with a name that nothing in the repository defines are not listed.",
